{title: I'm Headed For The Promised Land}
{artist: Larry Holder}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

Verse 1
and let me know what you think of this song or this method
of outreach.

Verse 2
Mark is a computer programmer and composer in London, England.
He wrote the music and sequenced the MIDI, and I added the words.
Mark plans to build a website for his songs, and til then I'll
host our collaborations here. This is our second collaboration.

Verse 3
I'M HEADED FOR THE PROMISED LAND
Music by Mark Wilkinson, Words by Larry Holder
Copyright (C) 1998 Mark Wilkinson and Larry Holder

Verse 4
Day by day,
I am headed for the Promised Land.
Born from above,
I am headed for the Promised Land!
By the mercy of God,
I am safe within the power of His hand.
Day by day,
I am headed for the Promised Land!

Verse 5
Though today, I cannot see Him,
In my heart, I know He's there.
One day soon, I'll rise to greet Him;
All at once He'll appear!
Til He comes, I will tell of Jesus,
Tell the world of His love.
Tell them how they can come to know Him,
How they, too, can be born from above!

Verse 6
Day by day,
I am headed for the Promised Land.
Born from above,
And by grace I fin'lly understand,
By the mercy of God,
I am safe within the power of His hand.
One fine day,
I'll see Jesus in the Promised Land!

Verse 7
Though the world, they cannot see Him,
Though they mock the words I say,
Still I know, He reigns in glory;
He's the Life and the Way!
Til He comes, I will tell of Jesus,
How He died for my sin,
Tell them how they can live forever,
How they, too, can be born again!

Verse 8
Day by day,
I am headed for the Promised Land.
Born from above,
I am headed for the Promised Land!
By the mercy of God,
I am safe within the power of His hand.
Praise His Name,
I am headed for the Promised Land!
